fibration and $f$ a weak homotopy equivalence, we show $\bar f$ is a weak
homotopy equivalence. Fix $e'\in E'$ with image $e=\bar f(e')\in E$,
$b'=p'(e')\in B'$, $b=p(e)=f(b')\in B$. The fiber $F'=p'^{-1}(b')$ identifies
with $F=p^{-1}(b)$ (both are ${(e,b')\in E\times B' : p(e)=f(b')}$ and ${e\in
E:p(e)=b}$ respectively, via the pullback). Under this identification the map onfibers $F'\to F$ induced by $\bar f$ is the identity. The Serre fibrations $p'$ and $p$ yield long exact sequences of homotopy groups, and the map $f:B'\to B$
induces isomorphisms $\pi_n(B',b')\xrightarrow{\sim}\pi_n(B,b)$ for all $n$
(since $f$ is a weak equivalence). The five lemma applied to the map of long
exact sequences gives $\pi_n(E',e')\xrightarrow{\sim}\pi_n(E,e)$ for all $n$ andall basepoints $e'$. Hence $\bar f$ is a weak homotopy equivalence. $\square$


